# 1e999 overflows float; strtof flags it with ERANGE as a side effect but
# still returns a usable (infinite) value, so GMANRIBTokenize::parseNum
# returns a REAL token rather than throwing. Without parseNum resetting
# errno before its own strtol attempt, that leftover ERANGE would wrongly
# poison the very next integer literal -- Sides 4 here -- with a spurious
# RIE_RANGE. Nothing else in this fixture set creates a pending ERANGE for
# a later integer to trip over.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 1e999
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
Sides 4
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
